#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# matrix_plot

#% text
# `matrix_plot(m)` draws a matrix as cells coloured from blue (negative) through white (0) to red (positive), with row and column numbers.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Row 1 is at the top; the colours are scaled by the largest absolute value.

#% item
# Options: `color_function` (a gradient from the least to the greatest value), and the options of `graphics`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A small matrix:

#% cell
matrix_plot([[1, -2], [3, 0.5]])
#% output
#= image("matrix_plot.files/matrix_plot-1.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A larger one:

#% cell
matrix_plot(table(sin(i*j/10), i, 30, j, 30))
#% output
#= image("matrix_plot.files/matrix_plot-2.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# With another gradient:

#% cell
matrix_plot(table(i - j, i, 6, j, 6), color_function: thermal)
#% output
#= image("matrix_plot.files/matrix_plot-3.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `array_plot`, `list_density_plot`
